---
// src/pages/_site-updates/2026-10-03-waitlist-phone-optional.astro
export const updateMeta = {
  date: '2026-10-03',
  title: 'Waitlist phone number is optional unless a call or text is requested',
  tags: ['waitlist', 'lead-capture', 'sms'],
};
---
<article class="border-l-4 border-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] pl-6">
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">October 3, 2026</h2>
  <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-4">
    The Founders application at
    <a href="/pricing" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">/pricing</a> no longer
    requires a phone number. An applicant who picks email as the best way to reach them can apply
    without one.
  </p>

  <div class="mb-4">
    <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1">Why</h3>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
      Agreement to receive text messages has to be freely given, so a phone number cannot be the
      price of applying. A number is needed only when the applicant asks to be reached by phone
      call or text, because that request cannot be honored without one.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1">How it works</h3>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
      The Phone / WhatsApp field is tagged Optional and switches to required when "Phone call" or
      "Text / SMS" is chosen, with an inline message if it is left empty. <code>/api/contact</code>
      enforces the same rule, and any number that is supplied is still checked as a real phone
      number. The text message consent box is unchanged and is recorded only alongside a number.
    </p>
  </div>
</article>
